tic by about six points. Bailey has leaned on attacks over the SAFE-T Act and crime, though crime numbers have fallen, and he received a surprise endorsement from President Trump in mid-September.\n\nEvery major race rater calls the contest Solid or Safe Democratic, and prediction markets price Pritzker's chances near 97 percent. The one available poll, from November 2025, showed Pritzker ahead 54 to 34. The main open questions are turnout in Chicago and the suburbs and whether Bailey can consolidate downstate support enough to cut into Pritzker's margin.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.98, "margin": 13.88}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.9829, "margin": 14.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.983, "margin": 14.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.9789, "margin": 14.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.9753, "margin": 14.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.9721, "margin": 13.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.9755, "margin": 13.9}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.9748, "margin": 13.5}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.9823, "margin": 14.5}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.9825, "margin": 14.5}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.9825, "margin": 14.5}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.9786, "margin": 14.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.9788, "margin": 14.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.9803, "margin": 14.5}]}